	<true/>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Kani uses the camera when you scan a menu, sign or page to read and translate it. The photo stays on your phone.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Kani uses your approximate location only when you ask for places near you.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Kani listens only when you tap Say it, to check how you said a phrase.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Kani opens the photo you choose to read and translate its text. The photo stays on your phone.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Kani turns what you say into text to check your pronunciation.</string>
